  "name_key": "category.strap_on_booster.name",
  "design_section": "7.11",
  "design_notes": [
    "Cost is printed per booster (\"$6 M each\"): stats.cost_each_M holds that figure and game.cost_M the total for the option (2 × 6 = 12, 4 × 6 = 24, 2 × 40 = 80). None is \"$0\".",
    "Burn \"~90 s\", thrust \"~12,500\" and mass \"~590 t\" are stored without the tilde. Thrust, burn time and mass are tagged real_world_approximate (7.0: thrust is rounded from the hardware class named in Twin); costs are game values.",
    "Liquid side boosters: \"= first stage\" in the three stat columns is mirrors_first_stage true, \"2× first-stage cost\" is cost_first_stage_mult 2 with no cost_M. \"Complex integration (+15 days)\" is game.integ_days 15 and \"reliability −1%\" is reliability add −0.01 on the vehicle (percentage points).",
    "Flags for cells without a number: increased_vibration (\"rough ride (vibration +)\"), staging_minigame_harder (\"more separation events\"), side_boosters_recoverable (\"recoverable (dual landing!)\"), cannot_throttle and cannot_shut_down.",
    "The 4 × small solid row lists only \"more separation events\" as its drawback. It is the same motor as the 2 × option, so it carries the cannot_throttle and cannot_shut_down flags too, while its drawback texts stay as printed. The heavy solid row says only \"can't shut down once lit\".",
    "The table has no lead time, integration days (except the liquid boosters) or reliability.",
    "No contracts list: \"massive thrust for lunar/Mars contracts\" is a strength, not a restriction. The None option has no twin and no model."
  ],
